<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We must show that for every object $C \in \calC $, the composite map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (\calC ^0_{/C})^{\triangleright } \rightarrow (\calC _{/C})^{\triangleright } \stackrel{G}{\rightarrow } \calC \stackrel{F}{\rightarrow } \calD  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is a colimit diagram in $\calD $. Lemma <a href="/tag/D7B730" data-tag="D7B730">5.1.4.4</a> guarantees that $\calC ^0_{/C} \subseteq \calC _{/C}$ is an idempotent completion, and therefore cofinal by Lemma <a href="/tag/215974" data-tag="215974">5.1.4.6</a>. Consequently, it suffices prove that $F \circ G$ is a colimit diagram, which is obvious. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>